{
  "task_description": "{'component_name': 'Main Container for TripFusion', 'description': 'Primary container for TripFusion implementation: A travel planning application that integrates with popular services like Google Maps, Skyscanner, and Booking.com to help users plan trips, discover attractions, and book accommodations or flights. It also generates AI-powered day-by-day itineraries for personalized travel experiences.', 'framework': 'react', 'platform': 'web', 'container': '{\n  "name": "ColorCraft frontend Container",\n  "features": [\n    {\n      "name": "User Inputs:",\n      "description": "Destination Travel dates Interests (e.g., nature, food, history) Budget (optional)",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Core Features:",\n      "description": "Suggest places to visit (Google Maps API) Find flights (Skyscanner API) Find hotels (Booking.com ) Generate itinerary",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Phase 2: Set Up Your Development Environment",\n      "description": "Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript (or React) Backend: Python (Flask or FastAPI) Database: Firebase or SQLite (for storing user preferences) Hosting: Replit, Vercel, or Render",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Phase 3: Integrate APIs",\n      "description": "1. Google Maps API Use Places API to find tourist attractions, restaurants, etc. Use Maps Embed API to show maps in your app. \\u2705 2. Skyscanner API Use it to search for flights based on user input. You can access it via RapidAPI. \\u2705 3. Booking.com API (optional) Use it to fetch hotel listings. Available via RapidAPI. \\u2705 4. OpenAI API Use it to generate a personalized itinerary. Prompt example: \\u201cCreate a 3-day travel itinerary for a solo traveler visiting Tokyo who loves food and culture.\\u201d",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Phase 4: Build the App",\n      "description": "\\ud83e\\uddf1 Backend (Flask or FastAPI) Create endpoints: /search-flights /search-hotels /get-places /generate-itinerary \\ud83c\\udfa8 Frontend Simple form to collect user input Display: Flight options Hotel options Map with pins AI-generated itinerary",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Phase 5: Bonus Features",\n      "description": "Save itineraries to user profile Share itinerary via email or WhatsApp Add weather forecast (OpenWeatherMap API) Add currency converter (ExchangeRate API)",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Phase 6: Launch & Iterate",\n      "description": "Host your app on githubShare with friends for feedback Add more cities, languages, or personalization",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    }\n  ],\n  "techStack": {\n    "frontend": [\n      "React JS"\n    ],\n    "backend": [\n      "None"\n    ],\n    "language": [\n      "JavaScript (ES6+)"\n    ]\n  },\n  "colors": {\n    "primary": "#1976D2",\n    "secondary": "#43A047",\n    "accent": "#FFC107"\n  },\n  "theme": "light",\n  "layoutDescription": "The UI features a clean dashboard with a search bar at the top for destinations. Below, users see tabs for \'Plan Trip\', \'Itinerary\', \'Flights\', and \'Hotels\'. The main area displays a map view with points of interest, and a sidebar shows the generated itinerary. Booking and navigation options are accessible via prominent buttons."\n}'}",
